Z||000004||Jefrysuko||11-30-2001||03:38 PM||||Ok good.  The reason I asked was that I pulled into a parking place the other day and had my windshield wipers going.  I had a little wait for a bus so stopped the motor and put the key back to the accessory position so that I could listen to the radio.  The windshield wipers continued to operate and I found it strange.  The funny thing is that I have been driving a Fiero daily since 96 and this is the first time it happened at least as far as I can remember.<P>On a side note.  When you turn off the wipers in a Fiero they make one last swipe and it has always annoyed me.  In my most recent Fiero this does not happen.  This car has a different turn signal stalk for the past owner added an aftermarket cruise control.  Would this different stalk be the reason the wipers don't make a swipe when turned off?  Just curious.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pyric||12-01-2001||12:06 AM||||It depends.  Different model Fieros may have had different Wiper motors.  I can't say for sure... because all I've worked on is my 85.<P>But I do recall it doing that last swipe your talking about.<P>Is your latest Fiero a newer model year?||||reg||1
